 why=["Beaumont sits on the Neches River near the Gulf, surrounded by bayous, marshes and the Big Thicket, and it gets some of the heaviest rainfall in Texas. Hurricane Harvey in 2017 and Tropical Storm Imelda in 2019 both flooded large parts of the city, and every heavy rain fills ditches and low spots with standing water. The Jefferson County Mosquito Control District runs ground and aerial spraying to keep mosquito numbers down.",
      "The humid climate and flood-damaged wood make Beaumont tough termite country, and Formosan termites are established in Southeast Texas along with native species. Historic homes in the Oaks Historic District and Old Town have wood framing and pier foundations that both attack. American cockroaches, fire ants and roof rats are active nearly all year."],
